      "seed": 540206399,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1929646623,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1794563140027,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "VNI = a 24-bit network ID (about 16 million networks, versus 4096 for VLANs). VTEP = the VXLAN Tunnel Endpoint that wraps and unwraps; in Swarm each host's kernel\nis the VTEP.\nUDP source port varies per flow (entropy for load balancing); destination port is 4789.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "b22",
      "originalText": "VNI = a 24-bit network ID (about 16 million networks, versus 4096 for VLANs). VTEP = the VXLAN Tunnel Endpoint that wraps and unwraps; in Swarm each host's kernel is the VTEP.\nUDP source port varies per flow (entropy for load balancing); destination port is 4789.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
